Redact api_key/admin_api_key/ssl_keyfile_password from server info endpoints

Fixes CVE-2026-105245 (boo#1284214): /server_info (and the deprecated
/get_server_info alias), the gRPC bridge get_server_info, and
Engine.get_server_info() serialized the full ServerArgs via
resolved_dict(), exposing api_key, admin_api_key and
ssl_keyfile_password verbatim. With only --admin-api-key set,
/server_info is reachable anonymously (AuthLevel.NORMAL), so the
admin key leaked to unauthenticated callers; with both keys set, a
holder of either key could read the other.

Carried from sgl-project/sglang PR 30343 by Rejudge-F (unmerged as of
2026-10-12; closed by github-actions as stale, head commit
38787264b70c5d931abf95ddf29d494fe5a943a8). Rebased onto 0.5.21: upstream
wrote ServerArgs.redacted_asdict() around dataclasses.asdict(), but
0.5.21 serializes via ServerArgs.resolved_dict() (msgspec defstruct +
resolution pipeline), so redacted_asdict() here masks resolved_dict()
instead. The three call sites and SENSITIVE_FIELDS are otherwise the
same; the unit test from that PR is not carried (no pytest in %check).
---
 python/sglang/srt/entrypoints/engine.py      |  2 +-
 python/sglang/srt/entrypoints/grpc_bridge.py |  2 +-
 python/sglang/srt/entrypoints/http_server.py |  2 +-
 python/sglang/srt/server_args.py             | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 4 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/python/sglang/srt/server_args.py
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/server_args.py
@@ -265,6 +265,23 @@
             for field in record_fields(type(self))
         }
 
+    # Fields whose values are secrets and must never leave the process via
+    # introspection surfaces (/server_info, gRPC GetServerInfo, etc.).
+    SENSITIVE_FIELDS = ("api_key", "admin_api_key", "ssl_keyfile_password")
+
+    def redacted_asdict(self) -> dict[str, Any]:
+        """Like resolved_dict() but with secret fields masked.
+
+        Keys stay present (so consumers can still detect whether e.g. an
+        API key is configured), but any set value is replaced with
+        "****". Unset (None) values are left as None.
+        """
+        d = self.resolved_dict()
+        for key in self.SENSITIVE_FIELDS:
+            if d.get(key) is not None:
+                d[key] = "****"
+        return d
+
     LANGUAGE_MODEL_ONLY_ARCHITECTURES = (
         "MuseGlimmerForConditionalGeneration",
         "Cosmos3ForConditionalGeneration",
